#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"id2\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Mode-based indexing {#mode-based-indexing}"
msgstr "Pengindeksan berasaskan mod {#mode-based-indexing}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "All operator representations refer to the indices that their terms act upon as **modes**. A mode is simply an index identifying a fermionic degree of freedom in your system. The mapping from physical degrees of freedom (such as spatial orbitals, spin states, or other quantum numbers) to mode indices is left to the user, enabling maximum flexibility.\n"
msgstr "Semua perwakilan operator merujuk indeks yang dikenakan oleh sebutannya sebagai **mod**. Mod ialah sekadar indeks yang mengenal pasti satu darjah kebebasan fermionik dalam sistem anda. Pemetaan daripada darjah kebebasan fizikal (seperti orbital ruang, keadaan spin atau nombor kuantum lain) kepada indeks mod diserahkan kepada pengguna, sekali gus membolehkan fleksibiliti maksimum.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This abstraction is also present in the [`qiskit_fermions.circuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit#module-qiskit_fermions.circuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit\") module, where the [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") operates on a register of fermionic modes. In both the operator and circuit representations, modes provide a consistent, algebra-independent way to specify which degrees of freedom participate in a given operation.\n"
msgstr "Abstraksi ini juga terdapat dalam modul [`qiskit_fermions.circuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit#module-qiskit_fermions.circuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit\"), yang mana [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") beroperasi pada daftar mod fermionik. Dalam kedua-dua perwakilan operator dan litar, mod menyediakan cara yang konsisten dan bebas algebra untuk menentukan darjah kebebasan yang mengambil bahagian dalam sesuatu operasi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Important\" type=\"danger\">\n"
"  **Current implementations use spinless modes**: All operator representations currently provided by this module treat modes as spinless fermionic degrees of freedom. This means if your system has both spin-up and spin-down electrons or fermions, you must explicitly map them to distinct modes (for example, modes 0-3 for spin-up of four spatial orbitals, modes 4-7 for spin-down, or any other convention you choose).\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Penting\" type=\"danger\">\n"
"  **Pelaksanaan semasa menggunakan mod tanpa spin**: Semua perwakilan operator yang kini disediakan oleh modul ini menganggap mod sebagai darjah kebebasan fermionik tanpa spin. Ini bermakna jika sistem anda mempunyai elektron atau fermion spin-atas dan spin-bawah, anda mesti memetakannya secara eksplisit kepada mod yang berbeza (contohnya, mod 0-3 untuk spin-atas bagi empat orbital ruang, mod 4-7 untuk spin-bawah, atau mana-mana konvensyen lain yang anda pilih).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  This design keeps the core representations simple and general while avoiding imposing a specific spin-ordering convention. Utility modules like [`qiskit_fermions.operators.library`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-library#module-qiskit_fermions.operators.library \"qiskit_fermions.operators.library\") provide convenience functions (for example, [`FCIDump.from_file()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-library-fci-dump#qiskit_fermions.operators.library.FCIDump.from_file \"qiskit_fermions.operators.library.FCIDump.from_file\")) that handle such mappings for you when loading electronic structure data.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"  Reka bentuk ini memastikan perwakilan teras kekal ringkas dan umum sambil mengelak pengenaan konvensyen susunan spin tertentu. Modul utiliti seperti [`qiskit_fermions.operators.library`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-library#module-qiskit_fermions.operators.library \"qiskit_fermions.operators.library\") menyediakan fungsi kemudahan (contohnya, [`FCIDump.from_file()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-library-fci-dump#qiskit_fermions.operators.library.FCIDump.from_file \"qiskit_fermions.operators.library.FCIDump.from_file\")) yang mengendalikan pemetaan sedemikian untuk anda semasa memuatkan data struktur elektronik.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Hint\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  As the package evolves, spinful operator representations might be added that natively support spin degrees of freedom in their data model. These will be clearly distinguished from the current spinless implementations and will coexist with them in the module.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Petunjuk\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Apabila pakej ini berkembang, perwakilan operator berspin yang menyokong darjah kebebasan spin secara asli dalam model datanya mungkin ditambah. Perwakilan ini akan dibezakan dengan jelas daripada pelaksanaan tanpa spin semasa dan akan wujud bersama-samanya dalam modul.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"term-grouping\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Term grouping and commutation relationships {#term-grouping-and-commutation-relationships}"
msgstr "Pengumpulan sebutan dan hubungan kekomutan {#term-grouping-and-commutation-relationships}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Like the coefficients and mode indices, operators can optionally store a **groups array** that associates each term with a group index. By integrating grouping directly into the operator representation as part of the sparse data structure, grouping information naturally travels with the operator through transformations. This enables systematic structure usage, whether from physical properties, algebraic relationships, or problem-specific symmetries. The structured information can then be used in downstream operations like circuit synthesis and decomposition by using methods like [`OperatorTrait.split_out_groups()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.split_out_groups \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.split_out_groups\").\n"
msgstr "Seperti pekali dan indeks mod, operator boleh menyimpan **tatasusunan kumpulan** secara pilihan yang mengaitkan setiap sebutan dengan indeks kumpulan. Dengan mengintegrasikan pengumpulan terus ke dalam perwakilan operator sebagai sebahagian daripada struktur data jarang, maklumat pengumpulan secara semula jadi turut dibawa bersama operator melalui transformasi. Ini membolehkan penggunaan struktur secara sistematik, sama ada daripada sifat fizikal, hubungan algebra atau simetri khusus masalah. Maklumat berstruktur ini kemudian boleh digunakan dalam operasi hiliran seperti sintesis dan penguraian litar dengan menggunakan kaedah seperti [`OperatorTrait.split_out_groups()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.split_out_groups \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.split_out_groups\").\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For detailed guidance on how to group operator terms in your workflows, see the [grouping](grouping#grouping-explanation) guide.\n"
msgstr "Untuk panduan terperinci tentang cara mengumpulkan sebutan operator dalam aliran kerja anda, lihat panduan [pengumpulan](grouping#grouping-explanation).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"    >>> from qiskit_fermions.operators import MajoranaOperator, gamma\n"
"    >>> op = MajoranaOperator.from_dict({\n"
"    ...     (gamma(0, False),): 1.0,\n"
"    ...     (gamma(1, False),): 1.0,\n"
"    ...     (gamma(2, False), gamma(3, False)): 1.0\n"
"    ... })\n"
"    >>> # Assign group indices to terms\n"
"    >>> op.groups = [0, 0, 1]\n"
"    >>> # Partition operator by groups\n"
"    >>> grouped_ops = op.split_out_groups()\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    // Create operator with 3 terms\n"
"    QkComplex64 coeffs[3] = {{1.0, 0.0}, {1.0, 0.0}, {1.0, 0.0}};\n"
"    uint32_t modes[4] = {0, 1, 2, 3};\n"
"    uint32_t boundaries[4] = {0, 1, 2, 4};\n"
"    QfMajoranaOperator *op = qf_maj_op_new(3, 4, coeffs, modes, boundaries);\n"
msgstr ""
"    // Create operator with 3 terms\n"
"    QkComplex64 coeffs[3] = {{1.0, 0.0}, {1.0, 0.0}, {1.0, 0.0}};\n"
"    uint32_t modes[4] = {0, 1, 2, 3};\n"
"    uint32_t boundaries[4] = {0, 1, 2, 4};\n"
"    QfMajoranaOperator *op = qf_maj_op_new(3, 4, coeffs, modes, boundaries);\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    // Assign grouping information\n"
"    uint32_t groups[3] = {0, 0, 1};\n"
"    qf_maj_op_set_groups(op, groups, 3);\n"
msgstr ""
"    // Assign grouping information\n"
"    uint32_t groups[3] = {0, 0, 1};\n"
"    qf_maj_op_set_groups(op, groups, 3);\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    // Partition operator by groups\n"
"    QfMajoranaOperator *grouped_ops[2];\n"
"    qf_maj_op_split_out_groups(op, NULL, 0, grouped_ops);\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""
"    // Partition operator by groups\n"
"    QfMajoranaOperator *grouped_ops[2];\n"
"    qf_maj_op_split_out_groups(op, NULL, 0, grouped_ops);\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"id3\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Arithmetic and mathematical operations {#arithmetic-and-mathematical-operations}"
msgstr "Operasi aritmetik dan matematik {#arithmetic-and-mathematical-operations}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "All operators implement the [`OperatorTrait`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait\") protocol, which provides a unified set of operations across different operator types. This ensures that code written for one operator representation works uniformly with others. See [`qiskit_fermions.protocols`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/protocols#module-qiskit_fermions.protocols \"qiskit_fermions.protocols\") for how this protocol relates to the others this package defines.\n"
msgstr "Semua operator melaksanakan protokol [`OperatorTrait`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait\"), yang menyediakan set operasi bersatu merentasi pelbagai jenis operator. Ini memastikan kod yang ditulis untuk satu perwakilan operator berfungsi secara seragam dengan yang lain. Lihat [`qiskit_fermions.protocols`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/protocols#module-qiskit_fermions.protocols \"qiskit_fermions.protocols\") untuk mengetahui bagaimana protokol ini berkaitan dengan protokol lain yang ditakrifkan oleh pakej ini.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The protocol includes arithmetic operations (such as addition, multiplication, and composition), structural operations (term iteration, mode support analysis, relabeling), mathematical functions (normal ordering, simplification, equivalence checking), and more. See the [`OperatorTrait`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait\") documentation for a complete reference of all available operations.\n"
msgstr "Protokol ini merangkumi operasi aritmetik (seperti penambahan, pendaraban dan gubahan), operasi struktur (lelaran sebutan, analisis sokongan mod, pelabelan semula), fungsi matematik (tertib normal, pemudahan, semakan kesetaraan) dan banyak lagi. Lihat dokumentasi [`OperatorTrait`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait\") untuk rujukan lengkap semua operasi yang tersedia.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"    >>> from qiskit_fermions.operators import FermionOperator, cre, ann\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> # Construct a Hermitian operator: H = +0 -1 + +1 -0\n"
"    >>> op = FermionOperator.from_dict({\n"
"    ...     (cre(0), ann(1)): 1.0,\n"
"    ...     (cre(1), ann(0)): 1.0\n"
"    ... })\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> # Check if the operator is Hermitian\n"
"    >>> print(f\"Operator is Hermitian: {op.is_hermitian(atol=1e-10)}\")\n"
"    Operator is Hermitian: True\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    // Construct a Hermitian operator: H = +0 -1 + +1 -0\n"
"    QkComplex64 coeffs[2] = {{1.0, 0.0}, {1.0, 0.0}};\n"
"    bool actions[4] = {true, false, true, false};\n"
"    uint32_t modes[4] = {0, 1, 1, 0};\n"
"    uint32_t boundaries[3] = {0, 2, 4};\n"
"    QfFermionOperator *op = qf_ferm_op_new(2, 4, coeffs, actions, modes, boundaries);\n"
msgstr ""
"    // Construct a Hermitian operator: H = +0 -1 + +1 -0\n"
"    QkComplex64 coeffs[2] = {{1.0, 0.0}, {1.0, 0.0}};\n"
"    bool actions[4] = {true, false, true, false};\n"
"    uint32_t modes[4] = {0, 1, 1, 0};\n"
"    uint32_t boundaries[3] = {0, 2, 4};\n"
"    QfFermionOperator *op = qf_ferm_op_new(2, 4, coeffs, actions, modes, boundaries);\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    // Check if the operator is Hermitian\n"
"    bool is_hermitian = qf_ferm_op_is_hermitian(op, 1e-10);\n"
"    printf(\"Operator is Hermitian: %s\\n\", is_hermitian ? \"true\" : \"false\");\n"
msgstr ""
"    // Check if the operator is Hermitian\n"
"    bool is_hermitian = qf_ferm_op_is_hermitian(op, 1e-10);\n"
"    printf(\"Operator is Hermitian: %s\\n\", is_hermitian ? \"true\" : \"false\");\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    // Clean up\n"
"    qf_ferm_op_free(op);\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""
"    // Clean up\n"
"    qf_ferm_op_free(op);\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<DoqAdmonition type=\"note\" title=\"Note\">\n"
msgstr "<DoqAdmonition type=\"note\" title=\"Nota\">\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  [`is_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.is_hermitian \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.is_hermitian\") verifies that $H - H^\\dagger = 0$ by reducing that difference to a normal form and comparing it against [`zero()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.zero \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.zero\"). Spelled out in terms of the other protocol operations, it performs the following:\n"
msgstr "  [`is_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.is_hermitian \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.is_hermitian\") mengesahkan bahawa $H - H^\\dagger = 0$ dengan mengurangkan perbezaan itu kepada bentuk normal dan membandingkannya dengan [`zero()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.zero \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.zero\"). Dihuraikan dalam bentuk operasi protokol yang lain, ia melaksanakan perkara berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  The strength of this check depends on the operator type, because it depends on how completely that type’s normal form contracts adjacent generators. A `True` result is always reliable, but for some types a `False` result is conservative: see [`is_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.is_hermitian \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.is_hermitian\") for details.\n"
msgstr "  Kekuatan semakan ini bergantung pada jenis operator, kerana ia bergantung pada sejauh mana lengkap bentuk normal jenis tersebut mengecutkan penjana bersebelahan. Keputusan `True` sentiasa boleh dipercayai, tetapi bagi sesetengah jenis keputusan `False` bersifat konservatif: lihat [`is_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.is_hermitian \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.is_hermitian\") untuk butiran.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "</DoqAdmonition>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Important\" type=\"danger\">\n"
"  The example uses `atol=1e-10`. The `atol` (absolute tolerance) parameter specifies a threshold. Coefficients with magnitude smaller than `atol` are treated as zero and discarded. This is essential for numerical stability when comparing operators, since floating-point arithmetic can introduce small rounding errors that would otherwise prevent equivalent operators from being recognized as such.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Penting\" type=\"danger\">\n"
"  Contoh ini menggunakan `atol=1e-10`. Parameter `atol` (toleransi mutlak) menentukan satu ambang. Pekali dengan magnitud lebih kecil daripada `atol` dianggap sifar dan dibuang. Ini penting untuk kestabilan berangka apabila membandingkan operator, kerana aritmetik titik terapung boleh menimbulkan ralat pembundaran kecil yang sebaliknya menghalang operator setara daripada dikenali sedemikian.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Hint\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  While the [`OperatorTrait`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait\") protocol provides a common interface, individual operator implementations might offer additional convenience methods not part of the protocol. For example, [`FermionOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-fermion-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator\") and [`MajoranaOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-majorana-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.MajoranaOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.MajoranaOperator\") provide a `max_rank()` method that reports the length of their longest term. Always consult the API documentation for your operator type to discover all available functionality.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Petunjuk\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Walaupun protokol [`OperatorTrait`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait\") menyediakan antara muka sepunya, pelaksanaan operator tertentu mungkin menawarkan kaedah kemudahan tambahan yang bukan sebahagian daripada protokol. Contohnya, [`FermionOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-fermion-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator\") dan [`MajoranaOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-majorana-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.MajoranaOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.MajoranaOperator\") menyediakan kaedah `max_rank()` yang melaporkan panjang sebutan terpanjang mereka. Sentiasa rujuk dokumentasi API untuk jenis operator anda bagi mengetahui semua fungsi yang tersedia.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"operator-term-ordering\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Operator term ordering and normal forms {#operator-term-ordering-and-normal-forms}"
msgstr "Susunan sebutan operator dan bentuk normal {#operator-term-ordering-and-normal-forms}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A fundamental challenge in quantum operator algebra is that mathematically equivalent operators can be represented in many different ways, each with different implications for quantum algorithms. The same operator can be written in algebraically equivalent forms (for example, $a^\\dagger b$ can be expressed as $ba^\\dagger + [a^\\dagger,b]$), yet these representations lead to different behavior in circuit synthesis, simplification, and numerical algorithms.\n"
msgstr "Cabaran asas dalam algebra operator kuantum ialah operator yang setara secara matematik boleh diwakili dalam pelbagai cara, masing-masing dengan implikasi berbeza untuk algoritma kuantum. Operator yang sama boleh ditulis dalam bentuk yang setara secara algebra (contohnya, $a^\\dagger b$ boleh dinyatakan sebagai $ba^\\dagger + [a^\\dagger,b]$), namun perwakilan ini menghasilkan tingkah laku yang berbeza dalam sintesis litar, pemudahan dan algoritma berangka.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The operator representations support **normal ordering** operations that transform operators into algebra-specific canonical forms using commutation relations. This enables reliable comparisons (two equivalent operators have identical normal-ordered forms), reveals simplifications (commutation relations cause terms to cancel or combine), and supports algorithms that require specific operator forms for correctness and efficiency.\n"
msgstr "Perwakilan operator menyokong operasi **tertib normal** yang mengubah operator kepada bentuk kanonik khusus algebra menggunakan hubungan kekomutan. Ini membolehkan perbandingan yang boleh dipercayai (dua operator setara mempunyai bentuk tertib normal yang sama), mendedahkan pemudahan (hubungan kekomutan menyebabkan sebutan saling membatalkan atau bergabung), dan menyokong algoritma yang memerlukan bentuk operator tertentu demi ketepatan dan kecekapan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Important\" type=\"danger\">\n"
"  Different operator representations might implement normal ordering based on different commutation relations appropriate to their algebra. For example, fermionic normal ordering uses anticommutation relations ($\\{c_i, c_j^\\dagger\\} = \\delta_{ij}$), while Majorana normal ordering uses different algebra conventions ($\\{\\gamma_i, \\gamma_j\\} = 2\\delta_{ij}$). Always consult the documentation for your operator type to understand how normal ordering is implemented.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Penting\" type=\"danger\">\n"
"  Perwakilan operator yang berbeza mungkin melaksanakan tertib normal berdasarkan hubungan kekomutan berbeza yang sesuai dengan algebra mereka. Contohnya, tertib normal fermionik menggunakan hubungan antikekomutan ($\\{c_i, c_j^\\dagger\\} = \\delta_{ij}$), manakala tertib normal Majorana menggunakan konvensyen algebra yang berbeza ($\\{\\gamma_i, \\gamma_j\\} = 2\\delta_{ij}$). Sentiasa rujuk dokumentasi untuk jenis operator anda bagi memahami cara tertib normal dilaksanakan.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"    >>> from qiskit_fermions.operators import FermionOperator, cre, ann\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> # Two different representations of the same operator\n"
"    >>> op1 = FermionOperator.from_dict({(ann(0), cre(0)): 1.0})\n"
"    >>> op2 = FermionOperator.from_dict({(): 1.0, (cre(0), ann(0)): -1.0})\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> # Direct comparison fails due to different forms\n"
"    >>> op1.equiv(op2, atol=1e-10)\n"
"    False\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> # Normal-order both and compare again\n"
"    >>> op1_normal = op1.normal_ordered()\n"
"    >>> op2_normal = op2.normal_ordered()\n"
"    >>> op1_normal.equiv(op2_normal, atol=1e-10)\n"
"    True\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
